  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-(x+2)(x-4)\\le 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-(x+2)(x-4)\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/12348273c26017bb59327a79b85a5b0fb3c0fc2f37583f7dd9ec30cfcb20b019.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 4.$",
